# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# This is a single-page app: every route is drawn by the client, so any path that isn't a real
# file must be served index.html rather than a 404. That includes /try, the read-only demo the
# website links to. 200 (not 301/302) so the URL the visitor sees stays put.
#
# /api/* is deliberately NOT rewritten. On a deployment that has the sync Worker, those paths are
# the Worker's; on one that doesn't, letting them 404 honestly is what tells the app there is no
# backend here, so it can stay quiet about cloud sync instead of prompting for it.
/api/*   /api/:splat   404
/*       /index.html   200
